WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:05.420
Eleven's secret connection to the monsters
of the Upside Down is finally revealed in

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.799
Season 4, with a huge twist.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:13.160
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and this
is the ending of Stranger Things Season 4

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:18.360
Part 1 explained, plus predictions and theories
for the second part and how to defeat Vecna.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.730
Spoilers, of course, so take care.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.000
The fourth season kicks off in horrific fashion
revealing that in 1979, there was a brutal

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.750
massacre at the Hawkins Lab, with Eleven the
only apparent survivor.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.890
This sets up the idea that El was the one
who carried out the attack.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:39.750
As the season unfolds and we see her smash
bully Angela in the face at the skating rink,

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:44.850
it's implied that Eleven was exacting revenge
on Two and the other test subjects who bullied

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:45.850
her.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.100
What if I am the monster?

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:49.890
Eleven's memories of that fateful day though
are missing.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:55.280
So, when she reunites with Papa and Dr Owens
at the Nina Project, she's able to re-experience

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:59.560
her early days at the lab and remembers one
of the orderlies who was friendly to her.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:04.970
It turns out that he's actually Number One,
and his special abilities were being suppressed

00:01:04.970 --> 00:01:07.220
via an implant in his neck.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:12.490
Unaware of this, Eleven pulls the implant
out, and he then uses his powers to lethal

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:15.710
effect on a team of guards who've come to
catch them.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:20.729
One also snaps the final guard's neck, just
like Eleven did in Season 1.

00:01:20.729 --> 00:01:21.729
We're alike.

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:24.190
You and I.
Eleven then discovers that it was One who

00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:28.850
slaughtered everyone at Hawkins Lab that day,
and the reveal is a double-twist because it

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:31.460
also turns out that he's Victor Creel's son,
Henry.

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:32.460
And though we don't see him till later on
in the season, early in the first episode,

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:33.460
Brenner mentions him by the name he goes by
at the lab, Peter.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:34.460
Peter, Alec, what's going on out there?

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.450
The Creels had moved to Hawkins in search
of a fresh start for their troubled boy who

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.430
teachers and doctors had all described as
"broken".

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:44.299
There he took an interest in a nest of Black
Widow spiders in the house, and his admiration

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:49.549
for them as predators and "gods of our world"
points to his megalomaniac desire to rule

00:01:49.549 --> 00:01:50.549
over and change the world.

00:01:50.549 --> 00:01:51.549
Humans are a unique type of pest, multiplying
and poisoning our world.

00:01:51.549 --> 00:01:52.549
I could not do that.

00:01:52.549 --> 00:01:53.549
And I realized I could make my own rules.

00:01:53.549 --> 00:01:54.549
I could restore balance to a broken world.

00:01:54.549 --> 00:01:55.549
A predator...
but for good.

00:01:55.549 --> 00:01:56.549
What's especially interesting is that Henry
already possessed powerful abilities before

00:01:56.549 --> 00:02:01.479
he even ended up in Hawkins Lab, and they
don't appear to be the result of any experiments.

00:02:01.479 --> 00:02:06.189
As he developed his psychic powers, he found
he could reach into people's memories and

00:02:06.189 --> 00:02:10.489
discover some of the terrible things they'd
done or experienced in their lives.

00:02:10.489 --> 00:02:16.060
This is similar to Eleven's abilities to perform
remote viewing on subjects across huge distances

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:21.040
such as the Russian spy in Season 1 or when
she reached into the memories of Billy's abusive

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:23.150
childhood in Season 3.

00:02:23.150 --> 00:02:27.620
Unlike Eleven though, the Creel boy decided
to use his power to punish his family for

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:32.230
what he saw as their transgressions, killing
his mother and sister, leaving the blame on

00:02:32.230 --> 00:02:35.159
his father who ended up locked away for murder.

00:02:35.159 --> 00:02:40.329
Henry was secretly sent to Hawkins Lab, where
Papa decided to exploit him to recreate his

00:02:40.329 --> 00:02:44.469
exceptional powers in others, branding him
with a Number One tattoo.

00:02:44.469 --> 00:02:48.750
Like many interesting villains, the show may
be trying to elicit some sympathy for him

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:52.959
when we see how the lab appears to be abusing
him with electro-shock torture.

00:02:52.959 --> 00:02:57.650
However, given One's murder of his family
and indiscriminate massacre at the lab, he's

00:02:57.650 --> 00:03:01.079
clearly delusional in his thinking that he's
doing good.

00:03:01.079 --> 00:03:05.739
And when he asks El, Darth Vader-style, to
join him to take down the evil Emperor Brenner...

00:03:05.739 --> 00:03:06.739
You are better than they are.

00:03:06.739 --> 00:03:09.420
That is why you frighten him.

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:13.249
We could reshape the world, remake it.

00:03:13.249 --> 00:03:14.249
Join me.

00:03:14.249 --> 00:03:15.249
No.

00:03:15.249 --> 00:03:19.889
As they face off, El tries to summon the power
to resist him, using the advice One gave her

00:03:19.889 --> 00:03:24.469
to recall a memory of something that made
her sad and angry, something similar to what

00:03:24.469 --> 00:03:26.809
Kali recommended to Eleven in Season 2.

00:03:26.809 --> 00:03:29.040
I want you to find something that angers you.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:32.969
So, it seems that One may have manipulated
Kali as well.

00:03:32.969 --> 00:03:38.340
The advice though isn't enough for the young
El to withstand One's incredibly strong powers

00:03:38.340 --> 00:03:43.340
and, as he's about to kill her, Eleven has
a memory of her own birth come flooding into

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:44.340
her brain.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.080
Jane, I love you.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:50.719
Instead of anger, it's this memory of love
which gives Eleven the strength to reverse

00:03:50.719 --> 00:03:55.739
One's imminent victory, and she smashes him
through the glass into the wall behind, and

00:03:55.739 --> 00:03:58.799
follows it with a nice little superhero landing.

00:03:58.799 --> 00:04:03.709
By the way, Brenner had already advised not
to give into anger a few days earlier.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:10.599
If you allow anger or emotion to invade your
thoughts, you will fail.

00:04:10.599 --> 00:04:15.329
The young El then dusts him into the Upside
Down, just like she did with the Demogorgon

00:04:15.329 --> 00:04:16.850
in Season 1.

00:04:16.850 --> 00:04:21.880
Both scenes are also an X-Men easter egg to
Jean Grey, who defeated the villain Mastermind

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:26.481
in this way, and the comic book in which that
happened was specifically referenced in the

00:04:26.481 --> 00:04:28.530
opening scene of the pilot episode.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.170
I'll take your X-Men 134!

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:35.370
It was also a cool detail how Eleven sent
One crashing through the mirrored glass into

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:39.470
the room behind, foreshadowing how, moments
later, she literally sends him through the

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:41.700
wall into another dimension.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:46.960
And as he tumbles down, bursts of lightning
strike his body, transforming him into Vecna.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:51.860
This big reveal that One is Vecna more or
less confirms a number of fan theories that

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:56.610
the original test subject at Hawkins Lab is
connected to the Upside Down and its various

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.070
villains like the Mind Flayer or the Demogorgon.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:04.490
And, similar to how the Mind Flayer monster
in Season 3 was created by melting and joining

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:09.740
together the bodies of its victims, One mentions
a couple of times how he seems to have absorbed

00:05:09.740 --> 00:05:11.040
the people he's killed.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.860
With each life I took, I grew stronger.

00:05:13.860 --> 00:05:15.620
They were becoming a part of me.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.780
They're not gone, Eleven.

00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.940
They're still with me.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:20.940
In here.

00:05:20.940 --> 00:05:25.290
In fact, Vecna sometimes asks his targets
or victims to join him as he tries to feed

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:30.280
off their misery or sorrow, which reminds
me a little of how Pennywise feeds off people's

00:05:30.280 --> 00:05:31.280
fear.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:32.280
We can also see some of the bodies he's collected
in the Upside Down version of the Creel House,

00:05:32.280 --> 00:05:33.280
such as Nancy's reporter colleague Fred.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.930
Vecna is also connected to the Upside Down's
hive mind, giving him the ability to spy with

00:05:35.930 --> 00:05:38.250
any of the monsters under his control.

00:05:38.250 --> 00:05:43.000
This is similar to how the Mind Flayer used
Will as a spy in Season 2 and Billy as a spy

00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:45.000
and pawn in Season 3.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.650
So when Steve, Nancy, Robin and Eddie cycle
through the Upside Down on their way to find

00:05:49.650 --> 00:05:55.250
the gate where Chrissy died, a Demobat spots
them and screeches, and we see Vecna reacting

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.000
as he can now track what the group are up
to.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.560
This is why when Nancy tries to go through
the gate to return to the real world, before

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:07.940
she can get across, Vecna is able to intercept
her by entering her consciousness and putting

00:06:07.940 --> 00:06:09.560
her under his curse.

00:06:09.560 --> 00:06:14.420
When Nancy falls into Vecna's lair, we can
see how the villain preys on his victims'

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:17.860
fear and guilt over the traumatic events in
their lives.

00:06:17.860 --> 00:06:22.810
So, for Nancy, she falls into the swimming
pool at Steve's house where Barb was killed

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.120
by the Demogorgon in Season 1.

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:30.031
This plays on Nancy's feelings of guilt about
how Barb died alone at the pool, while she

00:06:30.031 --> 00:06:32.490
was hooking up with Steve inside.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:37.570
Nancy is now mentally trapped by Vecna, akin
to what happened to Max when she visited Billy's

00:06:37.570 --> 00:06:38.570
grave.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:43.250
In that case, when Dustin and co played Max's
favourite song, it broke through to her, creating

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:46.050
an opening, an opportunity to escape.

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:50.500
Max combines that with recalling happy memories
of her time in Hawkins which gives her the

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.080
strength to break free of Vecna's grip.

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:58.300
I expect Nancy may need some similar help,
given that Vecna may also prey on her guilt

00:06:58.300 --> 00:07:03.810
over her re-kindled feelings for Steve, perhaps
accusing her of being unfaithful to Jonathan.

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:08.580
Ok, we have to talk about Hopper now that
Joyce and Murray have broken him out of the

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.530
Russian prison, and there's a huge clue in
Season 4 about how they'll return home now

00:07:12.530 --> 00:07:14.250
that Yuri's plane has crashed.

